course: dictionary
lesson: 8318
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dictionary often gives one word more than one meaning. Read the sentence first, then choose the meaning that fits the clues around the word. The word robot has three meanings: a machine that does jobs by itself, a person who acts without feeling, and, in South Africa, a traffic light.
explain: «A robot follows its steps exactly; a mistake in the steps is called a bug.» The clues are steps, mistake and bug, so robot means a machine that follows a program. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then put it in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some words change meaning from place to place. In South Africa, a friend might say, «Turn left at the robot.» The clue is turn left, so robot means a traffic light, not a machine. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: A robot is a machine that can do jobs by itself, following a program.
fact: Some robots move and act like a person or an animal.
fact: Robot can also mean a person who acts without feeling or thinking, like a machine.
fact: In South Africa, a robot is a traffic light.
fact: A mistake in a robot's steps is called a bug, and finding and fixing it is called debugging.
exercise: «A factory robot is controlled by a computer that drives motors in each joint.» What controls a factory robot? | A farmer | A traffic light | *A computer | A ball of wool
exercise: «A robot facing north that turns right once faces east.» Which way does the robot face after it turns right? | West | North | South | *East
exercise: A South African friend says, «Turn left at the robot.» What is the robot? | *A traffic light | A cow that walks into a shed | A machine that cleans floors | A person who never smiles
test: «A dairy cow can give 25 to 30 litres a day, and many are milked by robots that the cow walks into by herself.» What is the robot in this sentence? | *A machine that milks cows by itself | A farmer who never smiles | A traffic light | A cow that walks
test: Her teacher's voice was flat and cold, and her face showed no feeling at all, like a robot. What does robot mean here? | *A person who acts without feeling | A toy that jumps | A traffic light | A machine that follows a program
exam: «One robot replacing 10 packers takes jobs, but new jobs appear too, and people disagree about whether it balances out.» What do people disagree about? | Whether traffic lights are red | Whether robots can fly | *Whether automation balances out | Whether cows give milk
